==Enemy==
Even at 79 years old, this chimera of owl and pterosaur doesn't go down without a fight. Having stats on par with an [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] and a minor bonus of highly inconsistent [[Surge Attack|Surges]] (just 20% chance and Level 1), be prepared for anything too slow or long-ranged to enter Pterowl Hazuku's blind spot - which, ironically, is about the size of the regular Owlbrow's range - to suffer over 36k damage every ~5 seconds.

==Strategy==
Luckily, in all of Hazuku's appearances it barely has support or takes a long time to spawn (with the exception of [[Birth of True Man]]), making getting into its blind spot or rushing the enemies the best options. For getting into its blind spot, your best choices are [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] (with Move Speed Up [[Talents|Talent]]), [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and similar units. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] can also provide good support, and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]'s Behemoth Slayer ability allows it to cripple both Pterowl Hazuku and any [[Wild Doge]]s accompanying it. [[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]] is great against it as well, thanks to his decent health, Surge immunity, Behemoth Slayer, and strength against Floating enemies. Likewise, [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] specializing in melee and with enough speed also have no trouble getting within the blind spot. Pterowl Hazuku's Surge immunity matters little, as most [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attack Cats]] are completely unreliable against it anyways.

